WEBVTT

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:10.431
Hi there.

00:00:10.431 --> 00:00:14.191
Welcome to this video where we are going
to learn about cyberbullying.

00:00:14.911 --> 00:00:19.311
The goal of the video is to help you
to understand what cyberbullying is,

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:22.831
what motivates people to do it,
and how to recognize it.

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:27.391
In the video, firstly,
we will look at what cyberbullying is.

00:00:27.551 --> 00:00:31.039
Then we will look at some examples
of cyberbullying and what to do

00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:34.079
if you are being cyber bullied.

00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:39.151
What is cyberbullying?

00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:40.495
Cyberbullying is bullying

00:00:40.495 --> 00:00:43.823
that takes place through 
digital devices and online platforms.

00:00:44.335 --> 00:00:47.263
It involves sending, posting or sharing

00:00:47.263 --> 00:00:51.343
negative, harmful, false
or mean content about someone else,

00:00:51.503 --> 00:00:57.775
often with the intent to embarrass,
harass, or hurt them.

00:01:00.655 --> 00:01:03.327
Common forms include sending threatening

00:01:03.327 --> 00:01:07.647
or insulting messages through text,
social media or gaming platforms,

00:01:08.287 --> 00:01:12.735
spreading rumors or sharing embarrassing
photos or videos without consent.

00:01:13.455 --> 00:01:16.975
Impersonating someone online
to damage their reputation.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:20.574
Excluding someone 
from online groups or activities.

00:01:20.574 --> 00:01:24.734
Deliberately creating 
fake profiles to harass someone.

00:01:25.486 --> 00:01:28.846
Publicly posting hurtful comments 
or personal information.

00:01:34.286 --> 00:01:37.038
What makes cyberbullying 
particularly harmful

00:01:37.038 --> 00:01:40.958
compared to traditional bullying
is that it can happen 24/7.

00:01:41.006 --> 00:01:45.006
Reach a wide audience quickly,
be difficult to delete once posted,

00:01:45.118 --> 00:01:48.126
and sometimes allows 
bullies to remain anonymous.

00:01:48.494 --> 00:01:51.166
Victims may feel like there's no escape

00:01:51.166 --> 00:01:54.414
since it follows them into 
their homes and private spaces.

00:01:55.406 --> 00:01:59.486
For example, within a friendship group,
one student challenges others

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:03.726
to put a pot on the head, make a selfie,
and sends the photo in the chat.

00:02:04.558 --> 00:02:08.686
Then some of the group members
start bullying the others by calling them

00:02:08.766 --> 00:02:12.206
"potheads" on various occasions,
even on public chats.

00:02:13.182 --> 00:02:16.494
If you or someone you know
is experiencing cyberbullying,

00:02:16.542 --> 00:02:19.534
it's important to do the following things:

00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:23.230
Keep a record of the harassment, 
for example screenshots.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.910
Block the person.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.230
Report it to the platform.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.438
Talk to a trusted adult, 
school counselor or authority figure.

00:02:32.078 --> 00:02:36.750
Many schools and workplaces have specific
policies against cyber bullying,

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:40.237
and in severe cases,
it can have legal consequences.

00:02:41.053 --> 00:02:43.741
So in this short video,
we learned what cyber bullying is

00:02:43.741 --> 00:02:46.733
and looked at some 
examples of cyber bullying.

00:02:47.021 --> 00:02:50.253
We have also discussed what to do
if you are being cyber bullied.

00:02:51.101 --> 00:02:52.685
Thank you for watching.

00:02:52.685 --> 00:02:55.629
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.